    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UNLV1-Main-Campus-Las-Vegas/Research-Manager--UNLV-International-Gaming-Institute--FLEXIBLE-WORK-SCHEDULE-ELIGIBLE--R0153377-_R0153377": {
      "title": "Research Manager, UNLV International Gaming Institute (FLEXIBLE WORK SCHEDULE ELIGIBLE)[R0153377]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University of Nevada, Las Vegas (UNLV) appreciates your interest in employment. We ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application:   Once you start the application process you cannot save your work. Please ensure you have all required attachment(s) available to complete your application before you begin the process.   Required attachments are listed below on the posting. Your application will not be considered without the required attachments.   Please note that applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted.  If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact Human Resources at (702) 895-3504 or unlvjobs@unlv.edu . Job Description The University of Nevada, Las Vegas invites applications for Research Manager, UNLV International Gaming Institute (FLEXIBLE WORK SCHEDULE ELIGIBLE)[R0153377] ROLE of the POSITION Reporting to the IGI Director of Research, this position supports IGI's research mission through independent and collaborative work across the Institute's research portfolio. The role requires strong technical fluency in data science methods—including large-scale behavioral datasets, algorithmic auditing, machine learning, and reproducible data pipelines—alongside traditional research methods like surveys and qualitative analysis. Key responsibilities include leading manuscripts, white papers, and policy briefs; presenting findings to stakeholders and at conferences; writing grants and funding proposals; and supervising research staff (student workers, graduate assistants, postdocs). The Research Manager also supports editorial duties for the Gaming Research and Review Journal and assists with the Institute's triennial International Conference on Gambling and Risk Taking. BACKGROUND SCREENING Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background and/or credit check. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS This position requires a Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) from an accredited college or university as recognized by the United States Department of Education and/or the Council on Higher Education Accreditation (CHEA) in gaming, hospitality, computer science or other related field and 2-4 years of experience. Credentials must be obtained prior to the employment start date. Position also requires: Experience working with Institutional Review Boards (IRB) Experience with working in collaborative teams Experience working with large high-dimensional datasets Demonstrated accomplishment of organizing and executing research projects Proficiency in data analysis and research programming languages (e.g., Python, R) and experience building or maintaining research workflows Familiarity with data infrastructure and research computing environments (e.g., server administration, cloud platforms, version control, data pipelines). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Awareness of best practices relating to public and private funding for gambling research. Experience in submitting and acquiring grants and contracts. Ability to encourage and support entrepreneurial activity. Ability to work with technical experts (e.g., data engineers) to implement ideas, assign and supervise tasks, and provide guidance on executing data engineering and management tasks. COMMITMENT to DIVERSITY and CAMPUS VALUES A successful candidate will support diversity, equity, and inclusiveness and contribute to a respectful, positive work environment. They will use our Campus Values to guide their decisions and actions and demonstrate our Rebel spirit. SALARY Salary competitive with those at similarly situated institutions. BENEFITS OF WORKING AT UNLV Competitive total rewards package including: Paid time off, sick leave, and holidays Excellent health insurance including medical, dental and vision Comprehensive retirement plans and voluntary benefits programs No state income tax Tuition discounts at Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE) schools Tuition discounts for spouses, domestic partners, and dependents PERKS & PROGRAMS Employee recognition and appreciation programs UNLV athletics ticket discounts Statewide employee purchase program discounts RebelCard discounts on and off campus Wellness programming for all UNLV faculty and staff at no cost Opportunity for career advancements to leadership roles Connect with colleagues with shared interests Personal and professional development opportunities A comprehensive onboarding program, Rebels: Onboard Support and resources available for veteran applicants — contact  vetjobseekers@unlv.edu or visit our Veterans Webpage . HOW TO APPLY Submit a letter of interest, a detailed resume listing qualifications and experience, and the names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three professional references who may be contacted. References will not be contacted until the search chair notifies you in advance. Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience, with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications because this is the information on which the initial review of materials will be based. Materials should be addressed to Kasra Ghaharian , Search Committee Chair . Although this position will remain open until filled, review of candidates’ materials will begin on 09/08/2026. Applications must be submitted electronically through Workday. Please note that emailed materials will not be accepted. Veterans are encouraged to apply. UNLV values the skills of those who have served. Learn more at Veterans Webpage or contact vetjobseekers@unlv.edu for support. For assistance with the application process, please review instructions on How to Apply . For further assistance contact UNLV Human Resources at (702) 895-3504 or UNLVJobs@unlv.edu . SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS FOR INTERNAL NSHE CANDI